  "summary": "The drawing is internally consistent with an ATtiny-driven fan controller: an LM1117-5.0 (U3) regulates VCC to +5V for the MCU(s), the fan supply is switched high-side by a PMOS (Q2) with an NPN level-shifter (Q1) driven from PB4, I2C/ISP share the USI pins (SDA=PB0/NET0007, SCL=PB2/NET0005, MISO=PB1/NET0009, RST=NET0008), and a potentiometer feeds an analog input (PB3/NET0001). The two MCU symbols (U1 THT ATtiny45-20P and U2 SMD ATtiny13V-10S) are wired in parallel, matching the repository's documented SMD/THT alternative-footprint convention rather than a duplication error. Decoupling (C2/C3 100 nF), gate pull-up (R4 10 k), base/series resistors (1 k), and the 5V1 clamp (D2) all sit in electrically sensible positions, and no power rail is shorted to GND or to another rail. I could not find a deviation that the schematic actually supports, so no anomaly is reported."
}

